   - (b) a security interest in the Property Token or in the Beneficial Interest — in each case to the extent expressly granted by the debtor in an authenticated security agreement or equivalent signed electronic record satisfying UCC § 9-203 (see **Section 11.2**) — attaches, is perfected, has priority, and is enforced under Article 9 of the Uniform Commercial Code as personal-property collateral, and not under the law governing mortgages of, or foreclosure upon, real property (see **Sections 11.2 and 11.7**); and

   - (c) succession to the Beneficial Interest on the death of a Beneficiary is governed by the law governing intangible personal property and by **Section 7.6** of this Agreement.

1. The process for entering into this Agreement is as follows:

   1. The Grantor, or a third party instructed by the Grantor, creates the Trust by generating a Token ID using the function `generateId` on the Token Contract;

   2. the Grantor transfers the Property into the Trust by deed, or instructs a third party owner to do so, and records the deed with the relevant authority or recorder. The deed language shall specify both the Token Contract address and the Token ID, and shall name the grantee using the Trust Name stated in the Token Metadata (`definition.holdingEntity`) verbatim (in the trustee-of formulation where the conventions of the recording jurisdiction require it — see **Section 9.1**); the deed may also recite that the Trustee has full power and authority to convey and otherwise deal with title to the Property as this Agreement provides, and the absence of that recital does not affect the validity of the conveyance;

   3. the Grantor, or a third party instructed by the Grantor, Mints the Property Token through the Token Contract. This Agreement is attached to the Token Metadata via the `operatingAgreement` field. A copy of the conveyance deed may be attached to the Token Metadata to facilitate validation, but is not required for the Trust to be legally effective;

   4. Upon a Confirmed Transaction, the Beneficiary will be entitled to the Owner Rights (described below). Ownership records for the Property Token will be kept by the Token Contract.

1. The Trustee shall (the below Trustee powers and duties referred to herein as the "**Trustee Duties**"):

   1. act as the representative of the Trust at the behest of the Beneficiary, and manage the Property of the Trust consistent with the terms of this Agreement for the benefit of all Beneficial Interest Holders;

   2. hold, preserve, and defend title to the Property in the Trust throughout the life of the Trust, neither execute nor deliver any deed or other instrument transferring or encumbering the Property except as directed and authorized under this Agreement (**Sections 1.2 and 10** as to transfer and dissolution; **Section 6.1** as to encumbrances and recordable interests directed by the Beneficiary), and maintain the integrity of the corpus as **Section 1.5** provides, including by refusing any purported standalone addition to the Trust;

   3. prepare, execute, deliver, and, where this Agreement or applicable law requires recording, record any documents related to the continued existence of the Trust as well as in connection with any transfer of the Property Token or any termination event as defined in **Section 10**;

4. receive and act upon (or, where this Agreement so requires, decline to act upon) the notices, sworn certificates, recorded instruments, court orders, and other documents described in **Sections 8.2 and 10**, including verifying — on the basis of the records and evidence on which the Trustee is entitled to rely under **Section 8.2** — that the conditions precedent to any conveyance of the Property out of the Trust (**Section 1.2**) have been satisfied before executing any such conveyance;

   5. in connection with any dissolution of the Trust, perform the acts this Agreement requires of the Trustee, including execution and delivery of deeds in recordable form (**Sections 10.1, 10.2, 10.3, and 10.4**) and, where applicable, the distribution of proceeds described in **Section 10.7** (in a dissolution under **Section 10.5**, the wind-up functions described in **Section 10.5.2** are performed by the holder identified in that Section and not by the Trustee);

   6. have no duty or liability to the Grantor or Beneficiary with respect to any change in value of any of the Property during the life of the Trust, nor shall the Trustee be liable to any prior or subsequent beneficiary or trustee, except to the extent such liability is created by any private agreement or by the willful misconduct or gross negligence of the Trustee; and,

   7. not be required to furnish a bond or other security in any jurisdiction for the faithful performance of its duties.

5. Upon receipt of the sworn certificate described in **Section 10.2.4**, the Trustee shall, at the direction of the Beneficiary, execute and deliver a Deed of Distribution transferring the Property out of the Trust, naming as grantee the Beneficiary (or legal successor acting under **Section 10.3**) or the person designated in that person's direction. The Deed of Distribution shall be in recordable form and shall recite:

      - (a) the alternative dissolution provision under this **Section 10.2**;

      - (b) the recording information of the Notice of Lost Token Control;

      - (c) that the Quiet Period expired without any Confirmed Transaction initiated by the Account or Smart Wallet holding the Property Token and without any contest as described in **Section 10.2.2** (whether recorded or delivered), based on the Beneficiary's sworn certificate; and

      - (d) that the condition precedent in **Section 1.2(a)** and the signature requirement in **Section 10.1.2** do not apply to this Alternative Dissolution Event, the Notice of Lost Token Control and the expiration of the Quiet Period without contest serving as substitutes for those requirements.

   6. Upon recording of the Deed of Distribution, the Property Token shall become a Void Token.
